  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its first run (1 of the 6 allowed): all 7 witnesses pass and no other changes were needed.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_440_1_o3.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** any vehicle under the `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle` definition.\n- **When it applies:**\n  - the vehicle is on a highway and on the roadway lying on that highway;\n  - it is not in a business or residence district;\n  - it is stopped, judged by `drv_motion_stopped` with the `p.motion_speed_tolerance` setting;\n  - the exception does not hold. The exception is: the vehicle is disabled, it is on a roadway, and it cannot be moved.\n- **What it requires:** for every roadway the vehicle is on (picked the same way as above), the recorded sight distance is at least 200 ft, written as `Units.feet 200`.\n\n**One choice the node left open:** for \"a clear view … from a distance of 200 feet\" (span e10), I read \"the vehicle's place\" as each roadway it occupies. The sight distance checked is the one the source records for that roadway. I declared this as a narrowing on e10, so later sessions will see it.\n\n**Witnesses:** the car is on a highway with a roadway on it.\n- **forbid:** stopped in its lane, sight distance 40 m → violated.\n- **permit:** stopped in its lane, sight distance 300 m → compliant.\n- **idle:** moving at 15 m/s → doesn't apply.\n- **blind:** stopped, sight distance not recorded → unknown.\n\nI also added three extra test cases (`branch_1`–`branch_3`) so each part of the conditions affects at least one result. Each one should not apply, and none does:\n- in a business or residence district;\n- disabled and immovable on the roadway;\n- stopped on the highway but off the roadway.\n\nThe run log and these choices are in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
